most people have no idea what attachment  is and it really is the fundamental way  that one human being  connects to another human being and  that's based on everything that happens  to us from birth  when we're small our brain says that  everything that happens to me is my  fault and some of us grow out of that  most of us don't but a little brain if  someone neglects you  if someone doesn't pay attention to you  if someone hurts you abuses you if mom  is gone  10 hours a day and you're in the care of  strangers whatever it might be what  happens is the brain says there must be  something wrong with me  deep down inside that everyone else can  see but i can't i don't know what's  wrong with me but anyone who sees this  thing  they abandon me and reject me so i need  to put up a wall and never show anybody  what's secretly  really inside of me and i'll just live  my life that way  and so we act like cardboard cutouts to  other people we don't share our needs  with people we do 10 nice things for  them hoping they'll figure out what we  secretly want on the inside but we can  never show it  that's what attachment is
 

